## First, identify the Service:
kubectl get services

##Copy the actual Service name.
##Start port forwarding on EC2:

kubectl port-forward svc/YOUR_BAKERY_SERVICE_NAME 8081:80
Replace YOUR_BAKERY_SERVICE_NAME with the actual name.

For example, if the Service is named fairy-bake-fairy-bake-chart:
kubectl port-forward svc/fairy-bake-fairy-bake-chart 8081:80

Keep this terminal open.

Now, from Windows PowerShell, create an SSH tunnel:

ssh -i "C:\Users\Dell\Downloads\iot-project-key.pem" -L 8081:127.0.0.1:8081 ubuntu@ec2-65-0-99-2.ap-south-1.compute.amazonaws.com

Keep the SSH session open.

Open your browser and visit:

http://localhost:8081

You should see your custom bakery website.

